tokenx includes a tuning corpus (src/tune/corpus/) with excerpts of the
following texts. They keep their own licenses; everything else in this
package is MIT licensed.

- Team chat transcript (en): written for tokenx. MIT.
- Running-text paragraphs in French, Spanish, Polish, Czech, Russian, and Greek
  (src/tune/corpus/languages.ts): written for tokenx. MIT.
- Vite releases API response: GET /repos/vitejs/vite/releases?per_page=10 from
  the GitHub REST API. Release notes by Vite contributors, MIT.
- tokenx source code: src/index.ts, src/segments.ts, and src/types.ts of tokenx. MIT.
- Vite plugin API docs (en): docs/guide/api-plugin.md, https://github.com/vitejs/vite.
  MIT, VoidZero Inc. and Vite contributors.
- Cat article (ja): "ネコ", https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/ネコ.
  CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), Wikipedia contributors.
- Cat article (ko): "고양이", https://ko.wikipedia.org/wiki/고양이.
  CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), Wikipedia contributors.
- Cat article (zh): "猫", https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/猫 (zh-cn variant).
  CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), Wikipedia contributors.
- The Great Gatsby by F. Scott Fitzgerald (1925), Project Gutenberg 64317. Public domain.
- Die Verwandlung by Franz Kafka (1915), Project Gutenberg 22367. Public domain.

The Wikipedia excerpts were changed only by removing markup and joining
wrapped lines; the CC BY-SA 4.0 license applies to those excerpts.
